@startuml F1_BettingApp_Sequence_RaceProcessing

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequence {
  BackgroundColor #FEFEFE
  BorderColor #333333
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  ActorBorderColor #1B5E20
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3E5F5
  ParticipantBorderColor #6A1B9A
  ArrowColor #333333
}

title F1 Betting Application — Sequence Diagram: Race Result Processing (Background Job)\n

participant "⏱️ Scheduler/Timer\n(IHostedService)" as scheduler
participant "🏁 RaceResultWorker\n(Background Job)" as race_worker
participant "🌍 OpenF1 API\nClient" as openf1
participant "⚙️ Application Layer\nRaceService" as race_service
participant "🔧 Infrastructure\nRepository" as repo
participant "💾 Database\n(SQL Server)" as db

autonumber

note over scheduler
  Background Job Trigger:
  • Runs on schedule (e.g., every 5 mins)
  • Checks if race finished
  • Processes results automatically
  • No user interaction needed
end note

scheduler -> race_worker: 1. Trigger RaceResultWorker\n(Check for finished races)

race_worker -> repo: 2. GetAllAsync()\n(Races with status != ResultsProcessed)

repo -> db: 3. SELECT * FROM Races\nWHERE status != 'ResultsProcessed'\nAND date < NOW()

db --> repo: 4. Return list of races\nto process

repo --> race_worker: 5. Return races

loop For each finished race
  
  race_worker -> race_worker: 6. Check if race finished\n(date passed)
  
  alt Race not finished yet
    race_worker -> race_worker: 7. Skip race, continue
  else Race is finished
    
    race_worker -> openf1: 8. FetchRaceResults(raceId)\nfrom OpenF1 API
    
    note over openf1
      OpenF1 API:
      • External data source
      • Provides race results
      • Driver positions & times
      • Points awarded
    end note
    
    openf1 --> race_worker: 9. Return race results JSON\n{drivers, positions, points}
    
    race_worker -> race_worker: 10. Parse results
    
    race_worker -> race_service: 11. ProcessRaceResultsAsync(\n  raceId, results)
    
    note over race_service
      RaceService:
      • Update race status
      • Calculate bet payouts
      • Determine winners/losers
      • Process all bets
    end note
    
    race_service -> repo: 12. GetByIdAsync(raceId)
    repo -> db: 13. SELECT * FROM Races\nWHERE race_id = @raceId
    db --> repo: 14. Return Race
    repo --> race_service: 15. Return Race
    
    race_service -> repo: 16. GetAllAsync()\n(All bets for this race)
    repo -> db: 17. SELECT * FROM Bets\nWHERE race_id = @raceId\nAND status = 'Pending'
    db --> repo: 18. Return Bets
    repo --> race_service: 19. Return Bets
    
    loop For each bet on this race
      race_service -> race_service: 20. Determine if bet won\nCompare prediction vs actual result
      
      alt Prediction matches result
        race_service -> race_service: 21. Mark bet as WON
        race_service -> race_service: 22. Calculate points\nfrom odds
      else Prediction doesn't match
        race_service -> race_service: 23. Mark bet as LOST
      end
      
      race_service -> repo: 24. UpdateAsync(bet)
      repo -> db: 25. UPDATE Bets\nSET status = @status,\npoints = @points\nWHERE bet_id = @bet_id
      db --> repo: 26. Update successful
      repo --> race_service: 27. Confirmation
      
    end
    
    note over race_service
      Aggregated Results:
      • Total bets processed
      • Winners count
      • Total points distributed
    end note
    
    race_service -> repo: 28. UpdateAsync(race)\nSet status to ResultsProcessed
    repo -> db: 29. UPDATE Races\nSET status = 'ResultsProcessed'\nWHERE race_id = @race_id
    db --> repo: 30. Update successful
    repo --> race_service: 31. Return confirmation
    
    race_service --> race_worker: 32. Return processing result
    
  end
  
end

race_worker -> race_worker: 33. Log completion\n(Races processed: X)

note bottom
  **Background Processing Benefits:**
  • Non-blocking: Doesn't affect user interactions
  • Automatic: No manual processing needed
  • Scheduled: Runs at specific intervals
  • Transactional: Database consistency guaranteed
  • Auditable: Processing logged for analysis
  
  **Result Processing Flow:**
  1. Fetch finished races from database
  2. Poll OpenF1 API for official results
  3. For each bet, determine win/loss status
  4. Update bet records with status & points
  5. Update race status to ResultsProcessed
  6. User points automatically updated
end note

@enduml
